---

Third-party components bundled or optionally linked into binary distributions:

  pocketfft (BSD-3-Clause)
    Vendored single-header DSP library. Default FFT backend. Source at
    src/backend/third_party/pocketfft_hdronly.h.
    https://github.com/mreineck/pocketfft

  nlohmann/json (MIT)
    Vendored JSON parser. Source at src/backend/third_party/nlohmann/json.hpp.
    https://github.com/nlohmann/json

  miniaudio (MIT-0 / public domain dual-license)
    Vendored audio capture/playback. Source at src/backend/third_party/miniaudio.h.
    https://github.com/mackron/miniaudio

  FFTW3 (GPL v2-or-later, OR paid commercial license from MIT)
    Optional FFT backend, enabled via -DUSE_FFTW=ON. Not bundled. When linked,
    the resulting BINARY inherits GPL v2 terms — it cannot be redistributed
    under MIT. The project source remains MIT regardless of this flag.
    https://www.fftw.org/

  KFR (GPL v2-or-later, OR paid commercial license)
    Optional FFT backend, enabled via -DUSE_KFR=ON. Same caveat as FFTW: when
    linked, the resulting binary is GPL v2 and cannot be redistributed under
    MIT.
    https://github.com/kfrlib/kfr

  uWebSockets / uSockets (Apache 2.0)
    Optional WebSocket server, installed system-wide via setup.sh. When
    absent, a built-in fallback server is used.
    https://github.com/uNetworking/uWebSockets

  GoogleTest (BSD-3-Clause)
    Test framework, fetched at test-build time only. Not present in any
    shipped artifact.
    https://github.com/google/googletest

  Electron, React, and other npm dependencies — licensed under their
  respective terms as recorded in their package.json manifests.
